        <mxCell id="TlhWarUt8IobpmyEl58L-6" value="Similar to Query operation" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" parent="aDYkH86SO8wR03iJJXfE-21" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="760" width="274" height="111" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="274" height="111" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="TlhWarUt8IobpmyEl58L-2" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; font-size: 30px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 30px;&quot;&gt;What Caching changes in the system&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Other than adding and removing itens from the cache itself, adding a caching mechanism only warrents the change of replica&#39;s Query and Propagate methods, which will, potentially, make the payloads for thse operations much smaller.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fontSize=14;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="-1040" width="760" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pIC1x_s9uyH4CC-bbXb2-2" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Cache Using BitMasks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;extra space: O(n/64 ) /per node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;apply time: O(n/64)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Each node has a local id,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;This local_id is used to make bitmasks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Bitmask represents the parents (direct and indirect) of the node in question&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: initial; font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;The cache of a node is now just its bitmask and calculating which nodes needs to be sent (to clients or replicas) is as easy as doing xor on the cache and a given node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;The algorithm for determining which nodes can be the same&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="-720" width="710" height="380" as="geometry" />
